 the audio and the text  and so if i get tired of the uh  you know the somewhat dryer if you want  uh podcast on literature i can then go  into the movie so i've got enough what  looks to be enough interesting content  and there's other stuff in our library  uh i can always go back to reading the  chosen elbow there's no audio there i  got enough to keep it going so i know  that that whereas i was concerned with  korean that i wouldn't find enough  interesting content i now got more than  enough  an embarrassment of riches as we say the  only thing that's holding me back  is the russian  because this whole issue surrounding the  crime the crimean problem the ukrainian  problem which is not very much fun if  you're sitting in kiev or donetsk or or  the crimean worrying about your future  but it is an interesting  phenomenon to follow and there's so much  different news and commentary and and  stuff  and um you know and it also i'll just  finish on that you know we've got such a  great community at link um  i'm gonna be talking to two korean  members tomorrow  uh evgeny from st petersburg and then  elena from ukraine over the weekend  they're members who have created content  for us in russian on everything from  daily life to grammar to you name it  and they're very helpful and nice people  but i'm talking to sergey who lives in  belarus who's studying uh he speaks a  number of languages english german i  can't remember them all who's studying  italian  and he says you know i'm looking for a  kind of uh uh  interesting content that's not too  difficult have you got any suggestions  and i said well you should really try  the aleotto de la sera  from radio do an italian in italy  because they have these wonderful  podcasts on history and art and so many  different things  and so long behold i'm sitting at my  desk at five in the evening which is  probably six in the morning his time  and i get a little note my skype note  pops up in italian he says i've found  the alio